      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T10:11:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could this code just be:\n\n    final LinkedHashMap\u003cIpPrefix, Ipv6UpstreamRule\u003e upstreamRules \u003d\n            mIpv6UpstreamRules.remove(ipServer);\n    if (upstreamRules !\u003d null) {\n        for (Ipv6UpstreamRule rule: upstreamRules.values()) {\n            if (!mBpfCoordinatorShim.removeIpv6UpstreamRule(rule)) {\n                mLog.e(\"Failed to remove upstream IPv6 forwarding rule: \" + rule);\n            }\n        }\n        maybeClearLimit(mLastIpv6UpstreamIndex);\n    }\n\nthat would remove a map copy and some lookups and might run a bit faster.\n\nAlso, if you do this, do you need a removeIpv6UpstreamRule method at all? It\u0027s new in this CL, and I don\u0027t see any call to it other than here.",
